# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# aitu-backend — local data store (no database; see context/07-database.md)
# Policy: metadata is small and worth versioning, payloads are heavy and
# reproducible. So `metadata*.json` stays committed and the binaries do not.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Audio: always heavy, always re-downloadable or re-recordable.
aitu-backend/data/audio/**
# Matrices: binary .npz anywhere under data/ ...
aitu-backend/data/**/*.npz
# ... except the small committed samples used by tests and demos.
!aitu-backend/data/examples/**/*.npz
# Frame examples: the calibration and the hand annotations of one Synthesia
# screenshot are small, are read by hand and cannot be reproduced, so they are
# committed. The working-resolution copy beside them is written from the
# screenshot by one function and is not.
aitu-backend/data/frame-examples/cache/

